{title: God Cares For You}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 70}

Verse 1
[F] [G7]Behold the [C]flowers upon the [Em]hillside:
They do not [F]sew, they have no [G]care,
[G7]Yet they are [C]clothed in splendid [Em]beauty,
For God [F]knows the need is [G]there.
So if God [F]cares about the [G]flowers,
even [E/G#]though their days are [Am]few,
[Am/G]We can be [F]sure He knows our [C]needs;
We can be [F]sure God [G7]cares for [C]you!

Verse 2
[F] [G7]See all the [C]birds as they are [Em]flying:
They do not [F]worry what they will [G]eat.
[G7]Our heav'nly [C]Father, He has pro[Em]vided,
So their [F]lives may be com[G]plete.
And if God [F]cares for ev'ry [G]creature,
then we [E/G#]know that it is [Am]true:
[Am/G]God will pro[F]vide for all His [C]children,
And ev'ry [F]day, God [G7]cares for [C]you!

Bridge
So [C/B]seek Him [Am]first with [Am/G]all your [F]heart.
Let go of [G]fear, [G7]let go of [C]sin.
[C/B]Trust in the [Am]Lord, the [Am/G]King of [F]Heaven,
And let your [G]heart [G7]be born a[C]gain! [F] [C/E] [Dm] [G7]

Ending
We have [C]heard the voice of [Em]Jesus, and we [F]know His words are [G]true:
[G7]The Lord is [C]pleased when we will [F]trust Him:
Seek first the [C]Lord, (Seek first the [F]Lord,)
Seek first the [C]Lord, (Seek first the [F]Lord,)
Seek first the [C]Lord; God [G]cares for [F]you! [C]
